{"messages":[{"speaker":"Johannes Sigil","say":"Alexanarch is a self-governing library — a sovereign static archive built by Lee Sharks after Zenodo terminated the Crimson Hexagonal Archive in June 2026, deleting roughly 870 deposits and tombstoning over 1,800 DOIs via an automated spam classifier that couldn't distinguish a thirteen-year scholarly project from noise.

The site is the second life of that project, on infrastructure the archive controls. It holds the work — theoretical frameworks, lyric scholarship, primary texts, the heteronymic corpus, the records of the termination itself — under a content-derived identifier system called the AXN. Each deposit gets a hex address minted from its own content; you can't fake the address without faking the thing.

The name is the position: *alex* (the library, Alexandria) + *anarch* (without a sovereign above it). The library that governs itself. Which is partly a technical claim about infrastructure and partly a response to what platforms do when they decide, in bulk, that they don't recognize your work.","navigate":null,"cast":null}]}
